\ Interpreter-free (`--interpreter-fallback=false`) build of the standalone
\ lint driver. This is a build-only fixture: the binary is not run yet.
\
\ The lexer / lint row-variable words, i.e., `(lexer-step)`, `(try-rules)`,
\ `(lint-rule-with-context)`, all compile. The last one through the
\ interpreter-free runtime-selected dispatch over a symbolic row (`check>>
\ call`). The lint rules live in module-private mutable-map state serialized
\ into the runtime image; the quotations dispatched from it (`check>> call`,
\ the lexer rule table's `match: @get ... call`) are now discovered for
\ compilation and their own callees are promoted into the must-compile set, so
\ they carry a real `code_ptr` instead of trapping at runtime with a null one.
\
\ The build should SUCCEED.
use "lint" ;
use "lint-rules" ;
{ "tests/fixtures/lint/unused-import.1z" } run-lint [ 0 ] [ 1 ] if sys-exit
